From 60964fa8450409f9c748883904e294468fd6cca3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: HSS Mundur Polish <polish@example.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 05:09:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Polish pass: lightbox, entrance motion, mobile hero,
 robustness

UX
- Gallery: tiles open an accessible full-size lightbox (native <dialog>):
  prev/next buttons, arrow keys, swipe, Esc / backdrop to close, scroll lock,
  safe-area aware, fits portrait and landscape phones.
- Soft page fade between routes (app/template.js) and a short staggered hero
  entrance (CSS only; fully disabled for prefers-reduced-motion).
- Back-to-top button, "Get directions" button under the map, and the Little
  Kites link stays visible on desktop as a fallback for the iframe.

Layout
- Phone hero: eyebrow wraps cleanly, CTA buttons are full-width and stacked.
- Desktop hero: arch photo is sized from viewport height so the stats row is
  above the fold on common laptop screens (1366x768, 1440x900).

Robustness / SEO
- If the app bundle hasn't started within 5 s, scroll-reveal content is shown
  anyway (fx-fail failsafe) so nothing can stay invisible.
- schema.org School JSON-LD, apple-touch-icon, color-scheme: light so Android
  force-dark can't invert the design, branded tap highlight.
